## Part 2 Navigation

### Q6 — What did cd - do?

Commands:


$ cd /etc
$ pwd
$ cd ..
$ pwd
$ cd /var/log
$ pwd
$ cd -
$ pwd


Answer: cd - switches back to the previous working directory. It is useful for quickly moving between the current directory and the directory visited immediately before it.

